WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.173
This video shows cadences, the reusable series of follow-up messages that nudge a

00:00:06.173 --> 00:00:10.216
customer who stops replying to an automated text conversation.

00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:14.854
You will build one with a defined message and an AI-written message, and

00:00:14.854 --> 00:00:16.340
see how it is used.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.396
In an automated text conversation, customers often go quiet.

00:00:25.396 --> 00:00:28.570
One well-timed nudge can bring them back.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.467
A cadence is the list of nudges and the silence to wait before each one.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:39.350
You build it once and use it on as many automatic loads as you like.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.470
A customer who replies, or texts STOP, is never nudged.

00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:53.759
Open Interaction Center, Management, Cadences, and click Add cadence.

00:00:53.759 --> 00:00:56.269
Enter a name and a description.

00:00:56.269 --> 00:01:01.561
Leave Enabled ticked, because a disabled cadence never sends follow-ups.

00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:03.383
Click Add step.

00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:08.539
After minutes is how long the customer must stay silent, counted from the

00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:11.084
last message the automation sent.

00:01:11.084 --> 00:01:14.086
A defined message sends your exact text.

00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:17.153
Here, after an hour, a friendly check-in.

00:01:17.603 --> 00:01:19.158
Add a second step.

00:01:19.158 --> 00:01:24.600
For an AI-generated step, the AI writes the message from the conversation, and

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.608
the guidance is optional.

00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:30.236
Leave it empty to let the AI decide what to write.

00:01:30.236 --> 00:01:34.641
Here, after a further day, the AI offers two test-drive times.

00:01:34.641 --> 00:01:35.743
Click Save.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:43.369
The list shows each cadence with its number of steps.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:47.503
Open one to change its steps, collapse a step to read the others,

00:01:47.503 --> 00:01:51.113
or clear Enabled to stop it sending without deleting it.

00:01:51.113 --> 00:01:52.103
Click Save.

00:01:56.915 --> 00:02:01.614
Unlike campaigns, a cadence can be deleted, and you confirm first.

00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:07.748
Deleting or editing a cadence does not change conversations already in progress, because

00:02:07.748 --> 00:02:12.055
the cadence is copied onto each activity when its load runs.

00:02:16.255 --> 00:02:22.224
The clock restarts every time the automation sends a message, so the delays add up.

00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:26.515
Steps of 60 and 1440 send the first nudge after an hour of

00:02:26.515 --> 00:02:29.935
silence and the next one a further day later.

00:02:30.685 --> 00:02:34.918
The number of steps is the most nudges a customer will ever get.

00:02:34.918 --> 00:02:39.875
After the last one, the conversation ends on its normal no-response timeout.

00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:45.388
To use a cadence, pick it under Re-engagement on an Automatic activity load.

00:02:45.388 --> 00:02:49.629
Pick a business hours calendar on the same load to send nudges only

00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:52.765
while you are open, in the customer's time zone.

00:02:53.515 --> 00:02:58.076
A cadence is copied onto each activity when the load runs, so editing

00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:02.029
it later does not change conversations already in progress.

00:03:02.029 --> 00:03:06.955
Cadences can be deleted, and copied to another site with a deployment plan.

00:03:11.155 --> 00:03:14.465
Bring back leads who stopped replying to a text.

00:03:15.215 --> 00:03:19.585
Space nudges by hours or days, not all at once.

00:03:20.335 --> 00:03:23.795
Let the AI write each nudge from the conversation.

00:03:24.545 --> 00:03:27.445
Send nudges only during business hours.

00:03:29.445 --> 00:03:33.554
Build a cadence once, attach it to your automatic loads, and let the

00:03:33.554 --> 00:03:35.442
follow-ups run on their own.

00:03:35.442 --> 00:03:39.662
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

00:03:39.662 --> 00:03:41.105
Thanks for watching.

